Subject: Re: Complaint =E2=80=93 CA-2024-001342 (ref: 76334099)

=20

Dear Ms Walker,

=20

Thank you for your email acknowledging my letters of 20 Oct 2025, 21 Oct 20=
25, and 28 Oct 2025.

=20

For clarity, I am not challenging a judicial decision via the complaints ro=
ute. My complaint concerns HMCTS administrative failures and service provisi=
on under the Equality Act 2010 (ss.20, 29) and FPR Part 3A / PD3AA =E2=80=94 speci=
fically the revocation and non-maintenance of participation measures post-tr=
ial, the lack of adjustments when I was unrepresented and in clinical crisis=
, and the failure to respond substantively to my pre-action correspondence.

=20

Your reply states that =E2=80=9Cthis matter is at an end in this Court,=E2=80=9D citing=
 the 23 Dec 2024 refusal and the 4 Aug 2025 refusal. That goes to the judici=
al appeal pathway; it does not answer the administrative/service-failure iss=
ues raised in my complaint and pre-action letters. =20

=20

Accordingly, please treat this as a request for Stage 2 review by the Opera=
tions Manager named in your email (Mr Ray Harrison) and address the followin=
g service and equality points within 7 days:

=20
Policy & record: Was any HMCTS/RCJ policy, log, or decision record made whe=
n my participation measures were withdrawn post-trial? If so, please disclos=
e it. If not, please confirm none exists.
Continuing duty: What HMCTS process exists to ensure continuing compliance =
with FPR Part 3A after the conclusion of a trial (e.g., during orders/costs/=
drafting/appeal steps for a vulnerable litigant in person)?
Reasonable adjustments: Why were basic adjustments (intermediary support, s=
tructured communications, assistance with orders/costs timetable) not provid=
ed, despite notice of my Autism and PTSD and contemporaneous clinical eviden=
ce?
Equality assessment: Please confirm whether any Equality Act / reasonable-a=
djustment assessment was performed for the post-trial phase; if so, by whom =
and when (and please disclose it).
Remedial proposals: HMCTS=E2=80=99s proposed steps now =E2=80=94 including formal ackno=
wledgment of breach, apology, policy correction, and assurance of future com=
pliance, and how HMCTS proposes to engage with the MoJ regarding systemic le=
arning.
=20

I remain ready to provide updated medical evidence (including September=E2=80=93O=
ctober 2025 relapse) if required.

=20

Kind regards,

Nadia Zahmoul

Email: nadia@rosekross.com

Attachments (for ease of reference):

=E2=80=A2 Pre-Action Protocol Letter + Annex A (20 Oct 2025)

=E2=80=A2 Follow-Up Pre-Action Letter (21 Oct 2025)

=E2=80=A2 Urgent Escalation / non-response reminder (28 Oct 2025)

=20

=20

=20

=20

=20

=20

=20

From: HM Courts and Tribunals Service <replies@optic.justice.gov.uk>
Date: Tuesday, October 28, 2025 at 10:04=E2=80=AFAM
To: Nadia <nadia@rosekross.com>
Subject: Complaint - CA-2024-001342 (ref: 76334099)

=20

NOTE: Please do not edit the subject line when replying to this email.=20

=20

=20

Dear Ms Zahmoul

=20

Thank you for your recent Pre-Action Protocol Letter dated 20 October 2025,=
 follow up letter dated 21 October 2025 and follow up letter dated 28 Octobe=
r 2025

=20

I am the Delivery Manager and I am acknowledging receipt but responding wit=
hin our complaints process.

=20

The HMCTS complaints procedure is intended for complaints regarding adminis=
trative functions.  It is inappropriate to use the complaints procedure to c=
hallenge a judicial decision.

That saying, I see that you were informed as below on the 15 September 2025=
=20

=20

Your papers were referred to the Jurisdiction Lawyer, Mrs Levey, of the Cou=
rt of Appeal who has asked me to inform you of the following:

'I refer to the appellant's notice filed by you seeking permission to appea=
l the costs judgment of Mr Justice MacDonald dated 24 May 2024.

You have already sought permission to appeal the order dated 24 May 2024 ar=
ising from both the substantive judgment and costs judgment of Mr Justice Ma=
cDonald in this Court under case reference CA-2024-001342.

Your permission to appeal application was refused by order of Lord Justice =
Moylan on 23 December 2024.

Furthermore, your application for permission to re-open the decision of Lor=
d Justice Moylan dated 23 December 2024 was refused by Lady Justice King by =
order dated 4 August 2025.

As it is not possible to appeal the same decision twice in this Court, no a=
ction will be taken on your appellant's notice.

This matter is at an end in this Court.'

Master Meacher reviewed the above direction and you were informed that the =
contents was correct on 22 September 2025.

=20

Although clearly disappointing, this matter is now at an end and on this oc=
casion, I have found no evidence of maladministration.

=20

If you're unhappy with my response

HMCTS operates three stage complaints handling procedure. If you remain dis=
satisfied with our reply, you can ask a senior manager, Ray Harrison to revi=
ew your complaint by replying to this email/by writing to the below address.=
 You must explain simply and clearly what parts of the response you've recei=
ved you do not agree with and would like reviewed.

Mr Ray Harrison

Operations Manager

Civil Appeals Office

Royal Courts of Justice,

Strand, London=20

WC2A 2LL

You must explain simply and clearly what parts of the response you've recei=
ved you do not agree with and would like reviewed.

=20

=20

Yours sincerely,=20

S Walker

=20

Sharon Walker
Delivery Manager
RCJ Civil Appeals Office, Civil Appeals | HMCTS | Civil Appeals Office, Roy=
al Courts of Justice, Strand, London WC2A 2LL =20

=20

=20

=20

IMPORTANT NOTE: Please do not edit the subject line when replying to this e=
mail. Any emails sent to this email address (replies@optic.justice.gov.uk) t=
hat are not about your complaint will not reach their intended recipient and=
 won't be replied to. If you need to submit an application or require an upd=
ate on your case, this must be sent to the court or tribunal managing your c=
ase using their approved enquiries in-box. Contact details are available at =
Find a court or tribunal - GOV.UK (www.gov.uk).

=20


